  "narrative": {
    "text": "**Business & market dynamics:** The parking portfolio is showing early signs of an operational inflection, with a volume-led strategy lifting utilization and contract parking growth. Same‑location property performance improved despite overall revenue softness caused by asset sales. The stock trades at a deep discount to net asset value, reflecting persistent market skepticism, but that narrative is shifting: short interest has collapsed and institutional buying has increased, suggesting the bearish thesis is unwinding.\n\n**Management strategy and execution:** Leadership is pursuing a dual track—rotating non‑core assets to deleverage while executing a “volume first, rate second” operating playbook. Progress on asset sales and debt repayment has strengthened the balance sheet, and early traction in utilization and contract growth lends credibility to the strategy. Reiterated full‑year guidance signals confidence, though the widened net loss and ongoing portfolio reshaping underscore the transitional nature of the turnaround.",
